-- section 4.13 defer: read-at-exit semantics (NOT Go-style snapshotting)
-- @req: DEFER-01
-- @expected-pass-after: phase-32
-- A deferred statement reads its variables at SCOPE-EXIT time, not at the
-- `defer` registration site. Because the defer body is inline-lowered at the
-- exit edge, the `"{x}"` interpolation load runs after `x = 2`. Intended
-- stdout: `2` (NOT 1 — confirms read-at-exit, not argument snapshotting).
-- (`print` takes a String, so the Int x is printed via interpolation.)
-- Build+run fixture (WILL_FAIL in the check-only container).

func main() {
    var x = 1
    defer println("{x}")
    x = 2
}
